classDiagram
    direction LR

    class AuthUser {
        +UUID id
        +String email
        +DateTime created_at
    }

    class UserProfile {
        +UUID id
        +String first_name
        +String last_name
        +String phone
        +String avatar_url
        +Boolean is_driver
        +Boolean is_passenger
        +Decimal rating
        +String contact_preference
        +String govt_id_status
    }

    class Ride {
        +UUID id
        +UUID driver_id
        +String origin_city
        +String origin_address
        +Double origin_lat
        +Double origin_lng
        +String destination_city
        +String destination_address
        +Double destination_lat
        +Double destination_lng
        +DateTime departure_time
        +Integer available_seats
        +Decimal price_per_seat
        +String status
        +Boolean pets_allowed
        +String luggage_policy
        +Boolean instant_booking
    }

    class Booking {
        +UUID id
        +UUID ride_id
        +UUID passenger_id
        +Integer seats_booked
        +Decimal total_price
        +String pickup_location
        +String status
        +DateTime created_at
    }

    class UserPreferences {
        <<proposed, absent from current schema>>
        +UUID user_id
        +Boolean is_smoker
        +Boolean has_pet
        +Boolean has_large_luggage
        +String preferred_contact_method
    }

    AuthUser "1" --> "0..1" UserProfile : profile id
    UserProfile "1" --> "0..*" Ride : driver
    UserProfile "1" --> "0..*" Booking : passenger
    Ride "1" --> "0..*" Booking : reservations
    UserProfile "1" .. "0..1" UserPreferences : future preference profile

    note for UserProfile "Dans l'application, le modèle Dart AppUser correspond à public.profiles. Son id référence auth.users.id."
    note for Ride "Entité public.rides. Les coordonnées sont stockées séparément en latitude et longitude."
    note for Booking "Entité public.bookings. Le statut contrôle notamment les réservations confirmées."
    note for UserPreferences "Cette table n'existe pas dans les migrations actuelles. Les préférences du matching sont actuellement portées par PassengerRequest, en mémoire."
